    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. The audit output confirms the format works end-to-end: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, fiscal year `27`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, Luhn CHK `1`).\n\n**Changes, kept deliberately small and off the large classes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single read-only `memberId` property (regenerates the `OwnerDto` accordingly).\n2. **`CustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the small, standalone id-builder now composes `region + FY + HASH8 + Luhn(core)` and dedupes on the whole `memberId`. Reuses the existing `region()`/`hash8()` and the `FiscalYear`/`CheckDigit` utilities; added one tiny `fiscalYear()` helper.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a small `deriveMemberId` after-mapping and simplified `deriveLocality` to resolve the region directly (the same value the memberId carries), decoupling it from the id string format.\n4. **`OwnerCreateAuditAdvice.java`** / **`OwnerCreatedEventAdvice.java`** / **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the three audit emissions now reference `memberId`.\n5. **Deleted** `OwnerMembershipNumberAdvice.java` and `OwnerCheckDigitAdvice.java` (their derived fields no longer exist).\n\n**Structural-impact choices:** I left the large `Owner` entity and the DB schema untouched by reusing the existing `customer_code` storage column to hold the `memberId` value, and kept every edited method at cyclomatic complexity 1 (single-line label swaps and cohesive one-line additions), so no function or class was grown. The collision handling, fiscal-year value, audit records, and owner-segment/locality all now consistently reflect the `memberId`.\n\nNote: `util/CheckDigit.java` has a now-slightly-stale javadoc mentioning `customerCode`; I left it untouched (cosmetic only) rather than expand the change surface \u2014 say the word if you'd like it refreshed.",
